<html><head><title>Why</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><b>Empowering Teachers: navigating towards the future of education</b></span></font></p> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>In a dynamic and </span> <span>ever-changing</span> <span> society, higher education plays a crucial role: institutions must equip students with the skills and competencies essential for their own future and that of society.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span>As a teacher, you bear a great responsibility. Traditional teaching methods fall short in enhancing knowledge development, critical thinking, and long-term motivation. Moreover, the expansion of classroom education challenges meaningful teacher-student relationships. It can hinder the development of both less engaged and talented students.</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span>As we face these challenges, the call for broader perspectives on education grows. Transdisciplinary working methods offer promising answers. It provides you, as a teacher, with a platform to reconnect with students and develop essential, broad skills.</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span>With transdisciplinary co-creation - involving researchers, policymakers, entrepreneurs, and citizens - you can also work directly on complex issues and make societal impacts.</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span>Explore these issues and rewrite the future of education. Step by step, innovation by innovation.</span></font></p><p></p></body></html>